From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: mediatek: preserve ordering for CPU-to-WiFi HNAT GSO

Local TCP output reaches the CPU-to-WiFi HNAT path as non-linear GSO
skbs, typically containing 44 1460-byte segments.  do_hnat_cpu_to_ge()
currently reinjects the complete skb through the Ethernet QDMA engine,
where it is hardware-segmented before entering PPE and WED.

Client-side captures show that the resulting TCP and IPv4 sequences are
valid within each GSO batch but that consecutive batches are interleaved
on the PPE/WED output path.  The most common sequence holes are exactly
44 segments and multiples thereof.  Checksums remain valid, and the same
traffic is ordered when it bypasses HNAT.

Segment only CPU-to-WiFi GSO skbs in software before PPE reinjection.
Every resulting wire-sized skb still follows the existing HNAT, PPE and
WED path; routed forwarding and non-GSO traffic are unchanged.  This
also leaves the QDMA SG FPORT fix applicable to any non-linear segment
without relying on QDMA hardware TSO to preserve inter-batch ordering.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat_nf_hook.c | 28 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat_nf_hook.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat_nf_hook.c
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
 #include <net/udp.h>
 #include <net/netfilter/nf_conntrack.h>
 #include <net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_acct.h>
+#include <net/gso.h>
 #include "nf_hnat_mtk.h"
 #include "hnat.h"
 
@@ -1007,6 +1008,33 @@ static unsigned int do_hnat_cpu_to_ge(struct sk_buff *skb)
                 return -1;
 	if (unlikely(skb->mark == HNAT_EXCEPTION_TAG))
 				return -1;
+
+	/* QDMA hardware TSO does not preserve the order of consecutive GSO
+	 * batches after CPU-to-PPE reinjection.  Segment here while the skb
+	 * still has its original protocol and header metadata.  Each segment
+	 * is then prepared and submitted through the normal HNAT path below.
+	 */
+	if (skb_is_gso(skb)) {
+		struct sk_buff *segs, *seg, *next;
+		netdev_features_t features;
+
+		if (unlikely(!hnat_priv->g_ppdev) ||
+		    unlikely(!(hnat_priv->g_ppdev->flags & IFF_UP)))
+			return -1;
+
+		features = hnat_priv->g_ppdev->features & ~NETIF_F_GSO_MASK;
+		segs = skb_gso_segment(skb, features);
+		if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(segs))
+			return -1;
+
+		consume_skb(skb);
+		skb_list_walk_safe(segs, seg, next) {
+			skb_mark_not_on_list(seg);
+			if (unlikely(do_hnat_cpu_to_ge(seg)))
+				dev_kfree_skb_any(seg);
+		}
+		return 0;
+	}
 	if (unlikely(skb_headroom(skb) < (FOE_INFO_LEN + ETH_HLEN))) {
                 if(unlikely(skb_cow(skb, FOE_INFO_LEN + ETH_HLEN)))
                 return -1;
-- 
